<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::conflict_intensity" target="brazil_market_turmoil::investor_confidence" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising conflict intensity raises global geopolitical risk premia and triggers risk‑off flows that reduce both foreign and domestic investors' willingness to hold Brazilian assets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">brazil_market_turmoil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::conflict_intensity" target="brazil_market_turmoil::capital_outflow_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating regional fighting induces a global flight to safety and margin calls that prompt cross‑border investors to repatriate funds from emerging markets, increasing Brazil's net capital outflow rate.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">brazil_market_turmoil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::conflict_intensity" target="global_money_markets::risk_premia" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising kinetic activity and proxy strikes increase perceived sovereign, corporate and operational risk in the region, causing investors to demand wider credit spreads and higher equity/risk premia to compensate for elevated probability of losses and capital flight.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">global_money_markets</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::conflict_intensity" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_pressure_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Heightened Iranian regional fighting draws Western naval/air/missile‑defense assets and political attention toward the Middle East, degrading real‑time support and munitions flows to Ukraine and enabling Russia to increase kinetic pressure on the front.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::conflict_intensity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::geopolitical_trade_restr" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in Iranian regional military activity drives the US and partners to broaden sanctions and export controls tied to national-security concerns, producing tighter tech trade restrictions that spill into US–China controls.</data>
