<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::shipping_lane_disruption" target="brazil_market_turmoil::market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Disruptions in key maritime routes raise insurance and freight costs, delay Brazilian commodity shipments and create uncertainty over export receipts, provoking sharp repricing across equities, bonds and FX tied to Brazil and thus higher market volatility.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">brazil_market_turmoil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::shipping_lane_disruption" target="global_money_markets::market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute disruptions to key maritime corridors (e.g., Strait of Hormuz, Bab al-Mandeb) produce immediate uncertainty about commodity deliveries, insurance and rerouting costs and counterparty exposures, triggering rapid repricing and spikes in implied and realised volatility across commodity, FX and equity markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">global_money_markets</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::shipping_lane_disruption" target="russia_ukraine_war::tanker_movement_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">Kinetic attacks, mine threats and higher insurance/escort costs in key corridors (e.g., Strait of Hormuz, Bab el‑Mandeb) force rerouting, slower turns and cancelled sailings, directly reducing the volume and frequency of tanker voyages.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::shipping_lane_disruption" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::semiconductor_supply_cap" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased disruption of key maritime routes (Strait of Hormuz/Red Sea/Suez) delays or reroutes shipment of wafers, chemicals and fab equipment, forcing fabs into lower utilization and short-term capacity losses.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
