<edge source="global_money_markets::risk_premia" target="brazil_market_turmoil::capital_outflow_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in global risk premia makes emerging‑market exposures more costly or unattractive, prompting portfolio re‑allocations and forced selling that directly raise net capital outflows from Brazil.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_money_markets</data>
  <data key="d39">brazil_market_turmoil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_money_markets::risk_premia" target="iran_regional_escalation::energy_price_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in financial risk premia increases hedging and funding costs and triggers rapid reallocations out of commodity positions, reducing futures market liquidity and amplifying short‑term swings in oil and gas prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_money_markets</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_money_markets::risk_premia" target="iran_regional_escalation::shipping_lane_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher risk premia drive up war‑risk insurance and charter rates for vessels transiting high‑risk areas, prompting shippers to delay, reroute or reduce transits through Persian‑Gulf/Strait of Hormuz corridors and thereby increasing disruption metrics.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_money_markets</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_money_markets::risk_premia" target="russia_ukraine_war::market_access_restrictio" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising risk premia lead insurers, banks and commodity traders to raise margins, withdraw services or add restrictive onboarding requirements for counterparties perceived as higher risk, creating de facto regulatory and commercial barriers that reduce market access for Russian suppliers.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_money_markets</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_money_markets::risk_premia" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising risk premia raise required returns and depress valuations, reducing exit prospects and fundraising appetite for startups and thus directly cutting the flow of new capital into AI ventures.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_money_markets</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
